- The `Dog` class overrides this `sound()` method to print "Bark"

Now, when you call `sound()` inside the `displaySound()` method of the `Dog` class, Java uses **dynamic dispatch**. This means that even though you're calling `sound()` from within the `Dog` class, since `Dog` overrides the `sound()` method, the overridden version in `Dog` will be executed.

